Field discretization, boundaries and observables (@em-numerical-fields: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electromagnetism, #source "../sources/Understanding-FDTD-Schneider.lingua#r_3BTKKSTADJQXT1XD3S4WZVBMYM", #source "../sources/Meep-Methods-Manual.lingua#r_7V0TJSMDBGNHBD0MBTB94W8GRX", #electromagnetism "../../../inquiry/reproducible-computation/numerics/A-numerical-validation-study.lingua#r_7EY9S6DXHFHSJAGA30W35A4ZD8") { r_3HYVJQ7HP9QQG81XSQ8B5EDV3P
**Read:** [Understanding the Finite-Difference Time-Domain Method — John B. Schneider](../sources/Understanding-FDTD-Schneider.lingua#r_3BTKKSTADJQXT1XD3S4WZVBMYM), complete numerical-development chapters; [Meep — methods, tutorials, validation and licence](../sources/Meep-Methods-Manual.lingua#r_7V0TJSMDBGNHBD0MBTB94W8GRX), introduction, units, convergence and applicable tutorials.

A numerical field model approximates an explicitly stated continuous problem. Select geometry, units, material law, sources, initial/boundary conditions and the observable before selecting a solver. Finite differences, finite volumes, finite elements, boundary elements and spectral methods make different approximation and conservation choices.

Derive at least one discrete equation from an integral balance rather than immediately replacing derivatives by a stencil. Preserve charge/flux at material interfaces and distinguish point values from averages. State how geometry is represented and how singular sources or corners are regularized. Refining a mesh does not correct the wrong boundary condition or constitutive model.

Plan verification before fitting data: exact limits, manufactured solutions, independent formulations, conservation, symmetry, refinement and parameter sensitivity. Separate algebraic-solver tolerance from discretization, domain truncation, measurement and model discrepancy. A converged answer can still describe the wrong physical system. The next original Poisson, dielectric-stack and time-domain examples expose small problems completely enough to test independently. [Understanding the Finite-Difference Time-Domain Method — John B. Schneider](../sources/Understanding-FDTD-Schneider.lingua#r_3BTKKSTADJQXT1XD3S4WZVBMYM), [Meep — methods, tutorials, validation and licence](../sources/Meep-Methods-Manual.lingua#r_7V0TJSMDBGNHBD0MBTB94W8GRX) and the advanced studies then extend the reasoning to substantially larger electromagnetic calculations.

**Continue:** [Build a numerical validation argument across several kinds of evidence](../../../inquiry/reproducible-computation/numerics/A-numerical-validation-study.lingua#r_7EY9S6DXHFHSJAGA30W35A4ZD8).

**Return:** [Electromagnetism — charge, fields, matter, waves and physical evidence](../Electromagnetism.lingua#r_5TJPESCTTNAKY66JH2QNQYN1PY).
